<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ursus of Solothurn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 300</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Saint Ursus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orso-ipato">Ursus</a> of Solothurn is a Christian martyr who, according to tradition, belonged to the Theban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> and was executed at Solothurn with his companion Victor around 300. Their shrine became the religious centre of the town in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. Ursus is the patron saint of Solothurn, whose cathedral is dedicated to him and to Victor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ursus-of-solothurn.jpg" alt="Ursus of Solothurn" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Theban_Legion_Martyrs_-_Orthodox_Icon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
